<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"><title>Design exploration comparison</title>
<style>:root{font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;color:#171717;background:#f4f1e9}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0}a{color:#173f78}a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #a94600;outline-offset:4px}.skip{position:absolute;left:-999px}.skip:focus{left:1rem;top:1rem;background:#fff;padding:1rem}header,main,footer{max-width:1120px;margin:auto;padding:clamp(1.25rem,5vw,4rem)}header{border-bottom:4px solid #171717}h1{font:800 clamp(2.4rem,7vw,5.5rem)/.95 Georgia,serif;max-width:12ch}header p{font-size:1.15rem;max-width:68ch}.direction{display:grid;grid-template-columns:8rem 1fr;gap:2rem;padding:3rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #777}.rank{font:800 4rem Georgia;color:#5146a0}.facts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem 2rem}.facts div{border-top:2px solid;padding-top:.6rem}.facts dt{font-weight:800}.facts dd{margin:.25rem 0 0}.surface-links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.5rem 1rem;align-items:center;margin-top:1.25rem}.surface-links>a{min-height:44px;display:inline-flex;align-items:center}.visit{display:inline-flex;min-height:48px;align-items:center;margin-top:1.25rem;padding:.6rem 1rem;background:#171717;color:white;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none}@media(max-width:650px){.direction{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:.5rem}.facts{grid-template-columns:1fr}.rank{font-size:2rem}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){*{scroll-behavior:auto!important}}</style></head><body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to comparison</a><header><p>SpellingWords · isolated prototypes</p><h1>Three ways to make spelling feel clear.</h1><p>All directions use the Grade 2 <strong>Soft C and Soft G</strong> curriculum—city, giant, circus, place, face, race, ice, nice, page, cage, large, and change—so visual decisions can be compared against the same real material.</p></header><main id="main"><h2>Critical recommendation</h2><p><strong>Advance Direction A for further testing, but do not apply it to production yet.</strong> It best balances child appeal, practice focus, and a credible curriculum voice. Direction C is the safer fallback if dense reference use proves dominant; B should remain the expressive benchmark.</p>{directions.map(d => <article class="direction"><div class="rank" aria-label={`Rank ${d.rank}`}>#{d.rank}</div><div><h2>{d.name}</h2><p>{d.thesis}</p><dl class="facts"><div><dt>Palette</dt><dd>{d.palette}</dd></div><div><dt>Typography</dt><dd>{d.type}</dd></div><div><dt>Child appeal</dt><dd>{d.appeal}</dd></div><div><dt>Strengths</dt><dd>{d.strengths}</dd></div><div><dt>Weaknesses</dt><dd>{d.weaknesses}</dd></div><div><dt>Accessibility</dt><dd>{d.access}</dd></div><div><dt>Performance</dt><dd>{d.perf}</dd></div></dl><nav aria-label={`${d.name} surfaces`} class="surface-links"><a class="visit" href={d.href}>Homepage</a><a href={`${d.href}grade-hub.html`}>Grade hub</a><a href={`${d.href}skill.html`}>Skill reference</a><a href={`${d.href}practice.html`}>Question</a><a href={`${d.href}correct.html`}>Correct</a><a href={`${d.href}incorrect.html`}>Incorrect</a><a href={`${d.href}results.html`}>Results</a></nav></div></article>)}</main><footer><p>Exploration only. No production route or global style is changed.</p></footer></body></html>
